{"availability":"available","full":"kajica2/sainted-word-records","name":"sainted-word-records","description":"Sainted Word Records — audio-reactive video engine. Single-file, browser-native, MIT.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-23T00:10:15Z","updated":"2026-10-10T10:33:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sainted-word-records.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://sainted-word-records.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.309Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.309Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.309Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.309Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Audio-reactive video engine that lives in your browser. Drop a song, drop your clips, get a music video. 23 personas, 20 CSS filters, local-first, zero backend, your-footage-driven.","A browser-native, audio-reactive video engine for indie musicians, beatmakers, small labels, and live performers. The product exists because the current options for music-driven visuals split into three bad categories:","SWR is the fourth category: load your clips, drop in your song, the engine analyses the audio (BPM, key, beats, onsets, chromagram) and renders a real-time reactive composition with 23 persona presets, 5 character presets, and 20 stackable CSS filters. Output: WebM at 1080p (MP4 in v1.1)."],"features":["Template tools (Renderforest, VibeMV) — quick, generic, every visualizer looks the same","AI tools (Freebeat, Plazmapunk, Neural Frames) — novel footage, but not yours","Pro VJ (Resolume €799, TouchDesigner $600/yr, Notch $3,500/yr) — total control, 3-month learning curve","Adaptive beat detection — bass-energy tracker with adaptive threshold","Audio analysis v2 — zero-deps BPM (autocorrelation), key (Krumhansl-Schmuckler), chromagram, beat phase"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kajica2/sainted-word-record